  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "Perpendicular and oblique lines in the source orientation: actual a perpendicular c, p through B perpendicular c, a parallel p, and b oblique to c through B. Both original local right-angle elbows and the unnamed a/c foot are retained. The rejected assumption b parallel a belongs only to the proof prose.",
  "source": {
    "image": {
      "path": "ssot-resources/soviet10year-textbooks/artifacts/6-8g/figures/fig-205.png",
      "sha256": "69dcc2ae77d4bb23b47ca9ab3fe34941ccc3ce0aae8d30b7ef6063c77af7469b"
    },
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "geo68-c3-s1-n32",
        "text": "推论2．\n一条直线的垂线和斜线相交．"
      },
      {
        "lesson": "geo68-c3-s1-n32",
        "text": "证明．\n设直线$a$是直线$c$的垂线，直线$b$是直线$c$的斜线（图205）．\n经过直线$b$和$c$的交点$B$作直线$p$与直线$c$垂直．\n\n那么，直线$p$与直线$a$平行（见31节）．\n就是说，直线$b$不可能与直线$a$平行，因为否则经过点$B$可以有两条直线（$b$和$p$）与直线$a$平行，这与平行公理相矛盾．\n于是，直线$a$和直线$b$相交．\n\n■"
      }
    ],
